# Branch Freshness Check

Before beginning any implementation work, verify the current branch is up to date with `main`:

1. Run `git fetch origin main`
2. Run `git log HEAD..origin/main --oneline`
3. If commits exist that are not in the current branch, warn the user and recommend the following workflow:

## Recommended Catch-Up Workflow

If the branch has unpushed commits, recommend this sequence to incorporate upstream changes without merge commits in the PR:

1. `git reset --soft HEAD~N` — undo the N local commits, keeping all changes staged
2. `git stash` — stash the staged changes
3. `git pull origin main` — fast-forward the branch to match main
4. `git stash pop` — reapply the local changes on top of the updated branch
5. Resolve any conflicts, then re-commit

This keeps the PR history clean — only the user's work, no merge commits from catching up.

Do not execute this workflow automatically — present the situation and the steps, then let the user decide.
